---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Accessibility" description="Elvisfreg Nigeria Limited's accessibility statement for this website." path="/accessibility/">
  <div class="wrap pt-8">
    <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Accessibility' }]} />
  </div>
  <section class="wrap pt-10 pb-20 md:pt-14 md:pb-28 prose">
    <h1 class="h1">Accessibility</h1>
    <p class="text-[1.125rem] text-ink-muted">We want everyone to be able to use this site. It is built to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines 2.2 at level AA.</p>
    <p class="data text-ink-muted">Last reviewed 8 September 2026</p>

    <h2 class="h3">What we have done</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Text and background colours meet a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 in both the light and dark themes; every pairing was measured.</li>
      <li>Everything can be operated with a keyboard, with a visible focus indicator, and there is a skip link to the main content.</li>
      <li>Headings are in order, images have text alternatives, form fields have visible labels, and errors are announced and explained.</li>
      <li>Animation respects your system's reduced-motion setting; with it on, the site is static.</li>
      <li>Text can be enlarged to 200 percent without loss of content, and the site works on a 320-pixel-wide screen.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h3">Known limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The downloadable company profile is a PDF that may not be fully tagged for screen readers. Ask us and we will send the information in another form.</li>
      <li>Client logos are images supplied by those companies; each carries the company name as its text alternative.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h3">Tell us</h2>
    <p>If something on this site is hard to use, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="link">{SITE.email}</a> and say what you were trying to do. We will fix what we can and respond within 30 days.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
